From 3084372d3a84c757eaae69310558b10314369594 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Tarjan <github@paulisageek.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 18:54:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] Make Raiders'/Foray's food-and-or-resources split a real
 per-player choice

events::food_or_resources applied a fixed "resources first" formula to
Raiders' loss and Foray's gain, unconditionally, on the ordinary self-play
path -- not a rule, per RULES_SPEC.md 5.3 ("multiple-player decisions
resolve clockwise from the revealing player") and BGO journal evidence
(game 7522886: "Green choses first", then differing real splits for an
identical total-2 loss). Replace it with QueueItem::FoodOrResSplit /
ChoiceKind::FoodOrResSplit, opened exactly like decrease_population's
existing QueueItem::LosePop, enumerated by reusing plunder_split_options
for the loss side (self-directed instead of attacker-directed) and a new
food_or_res_gain_options for Foray's gain side. resolve_count_targets now
walks the clockwise revealer order for resolution, not the strength-sorted
selection order, when more than one player is targeted. pending_moves
already turns any open choice into scored Move::Choose candidates with no
ChoiceKind-specific code, so the weighted bot decides this split with its
ordinary evaluation, not a hardcoded heuristic.

replay_common.rs's post-hoc journal correction for this exact bug (patch
p.food/p.resources after the fact) is now dead, since nothing applies a
guess synchronously anymore; repointed resolve_intervening's drain match at
resolving the real choice against the same produces_grants/spends_grants
FIFOs instead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 0170f8fc8c317b00b9e32584e5186fc2c68f2cda)
