From 50502464f7a6f7fc6e6748842151a4e8a6821d3e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Tarjan <github@paulisageek.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 21:27:03 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Fix UNITS bugs in uprising and row_last_copy weighted
 features

uprising was a flat 0/1 indicator, so its single fitted coefficient had to
price a catastrophic mid-game uprising and an almost-free turn-1 one
identically -- the live climb log shows it pinned at the clamp trying to do
both. Scale it by the gross production (science+culture+food+resources)
RULES_SPEC 6.3 says the whole Production Phase actually forfeits, so the
same coefficient now means value-per-point-of-production-at-stake at every
board size.

row_last_copy summed card_potential(w)*gone -- a composite the LIVE weight
vector already prices -- then eval::evaluate multiplied that sum AGAIN by
row_last_copy's own coefficient, so that coefficient's fitted value drifted
every time an unrelated weight moved (weights.rs's own sign-intent audit
had flagged this and explicitly left it: "its defect is units, not sign").
card_potential is now used only as the existing >0.0 "is this card wanted"
gate; the sum is gone alone, a deterministic w-independent probability, so
eval::evaluate's rlc * row_last_copy(...) is the only weight this reading
depends on.

Both fixes add a test confirmed RED against the pre-fix formula. Full
`cargo test --profile difftest --lib`: 1339 passed, 0 failed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
