From 7f7b4f2b133fcd9c0352b6876ed8526c81d1f5a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Tarjan <github@paulisageek.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 20:16:21 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Extend card-pricing coverage: territory nested blocks +
 enum-exhaustive Special match

The existing coverage_of_printed_effect_keys module (commit b075860 et al)
audits only the TOP LEVEL of a card's `effects` JSON object, so it silently
skipped all 12 territory cards (their content lives in sibling
`immediateEffects`/`permanentEffects` keys instead) -- a real gap in the
CHECK, not the pricing, which card_yields already got right. Added
TERRITORY_PRICED_ELSEWHERE plus forward/reverse tests closing it.

Also added special_effect_key: an exhaustive match over `Special` itself
(no wildcard arm), transcribed from card_table.rs's own parser dispatch, so
a variant added to the enum is a compile error here before any card ever
prints it -- stronger than the existing string-keyed check, which only
trips once real data uses a key. every_special_value_on_a_real_card_maps_to_an_accounted_for_key
confirms every key it can produce today is registered.

No pricing gaps found: cargo test --profile difftest is 1533 passed, 0
failed across all 33 test result blocks.
---
 rust/src/bots/weighted/cards.rs | 299 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 298 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

